  "body": "## Change\n\nUse the specified bull-nose corner radius to check straight, upright cuts for a gouge in the native Envelope verifier. The check reports remaining stock as unmeasured.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The original native verifier missed the two R1 gouges. The patched verifier reports both. The tangent R1 rail and the R3 control remain free of gouges.\n- The independent oracle measured 0.100 mm of gouge for the lowered Ø8 R1 rail. The same-diameter ball had 0.193 mm of clearance.\n- The oracle measured 0.633 mm of vertical rest at the R3 test point. The native R3 result reports `RestUnjudged`.\n- The explicit and implicit ball profiles produce identical warnings on the same rail. The existing numeric ball-envelope test also passes.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Windows native quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) passed all six steps on `f48a9aaf6`. It ran 270 tests with zero failures or skips.\n- The native baseline ran the same three regression cases. All three failed as expected, and the ten existing tests passed.\n- The independent rail oracle passed all seven checks.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `bullnose_envelope::bullnose_envelope_catches_the_r1_gouge_that_the_ball_misses`\n- `bullnose_envelope::bullnose_envelope_distinguishes_r1_from_r3_on_the_same_rail`\n- `bullnose_envelope::bullnose_envelope_marks_the_r3_rail_rest_as_unmeasured`\n\n## Scope\n\nThe tests use synthetic parts and fixed upright axes. Bull-nose rest measurement, arc and tilted motion, and physical machining were outside this verification.\n\nThe issue branch starts at upstream commit `29bb9e9a2`, after cut `v0.26.0`.\n\nChangelog: The Envelope verifier detects gouges from straight, upright bull-nose cuts and reports remaining stock as unmeasured.\n\nRefs #1531\r\n",
